{"title":"Fermentation Technologist Roadmap","role":"Fermentation Technologist","summary":"A Fermentation Technologist develops, operates, monitors and optimises biological fermentation processes used to produce products such as enzymes, antibiotics, vaccines, organic acids, amino acids, biofuels, food ingredients, probiotics and recombinant proteins. The role combines biotechnology, microbiology, biochemistry, biochemical engineering, bioreactor design, downstream processing and process control.","facts":{},"about":[{"label":"Career-route check","text":"Direct alignment. Biotechnology Engineering provides a strong undergraduate foundation for fermentation and bioprocess careers. For advanced R&D, process-development and scientist positions, postgraduate specialisation can be highly valuable."}],"intro":[{"type":"table","header":["Item","Details"],"rows":[[{"text":"Starts"},{"text":"Year 1 UG · 2026"}],[{"text":"Current degree"},{"text":"B.Tech / B.E. Biotechnology Engineering"}],[{"text":"Desired career"},{"text":"Fermentation Technologist"}],[{"text":"Career cluster"},{"text":"Engineering & Technology"}],[{"text":"Primary route"},{"text":"Biotechnology Engineering → Fermentation/Bioprocessing → Process Development / Manufacturing"}],[{"text":"Core domains"},{"text":"Microbiology, biochemistry, fermentation, bioreactors, downstream processing, process control"}],[{"text":"Major industries"},{"text":"Biopharmaceuticals, food & beverages, industrial biotechnology, enzymes, biofuels, chemicals, nutraceuticals"}]]}],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Biotechnology fundamentals, microbiology laboratory skills, fermentation projects and industrial exposure"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Fermentation/process development, upstream processing, downstream processing or biopharmaceutical manufacturing"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Senior Fermentation/Proc